#### Scheduler Integration

The metronome click must fire inside the scheduler's `onStep` callback to be precisely timed with the lookahead buffer. The key question: where should the metronome decision live?

**Approach:** Add the metronome logic into the `onStep` callback in `useTransportStore.play()`. This is the natural location because the scheduler already fires `onStep` for every subdivision step. The metronome should only click on quarter-note boundaries, which are calculated from the step index and subdivision:

**File:** `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/drum-practice/src/lib/store/useTransportStore.ts`

Inside the `onStep` callback within `play()`:

```typescript
import { playMetronomeClick } from '../audio/MetronomeClick';
import { useSettingsStore } from './useSettingsStore';

const onStep = (step: number, time: number) => {
  // ... existing pattern playback logic ...

  // Metronome click logic
  const settings = useSettingsStore.getState();
  const metronomeMode = settings.metronomeMode;
  if (metronomeMode !== 'off') {
    const subdivision = livePattern.subdivision;
    const stepsPerBeat = subdivision === '8th' ? 2 : subdivision === '16th' ? 4 : 3;
    const totalSteps = livePattern.totalSteps;
    const beatsPerBar = totalSteps / stepsPerBeat;

    // Only click on quarter-note boundaries
    if (step % stepsPerBeat === 0) {
      const beatInBar = step / stepsPerBeat; // 0-based beat index within the bar

      let shouldClick = false;
      let isDownbeat = beatInBar === 0;

      switch (metronomeMode) {
        case 'every-beat':
          shouldClick = true;
          break;
        case '2-and-4':
          // beats 1 and 3 (0-indexed) in 4/4 = beats 2 and 4
          shouldClick = beatInBar === 1 || beatInBar === 3;
          isDownbeat = false; // 2-and-4 has no downbeat emphasis
          break;
        case 'one-per-bar':
          shouldClick = beatInBar === 0;
          break;
      }

      if (shouldClick) {
        playMetronomeClick(time, isDownbeat, settings.metronomeVolume);
      }
    }
  }
};
```

This avoids adding a separate step listener and keeps all audio scheduling in the same callback, which is the existing pattern.

