I now have a thorough understanding of the entire codebase. Let me provide the complete implementation plan.

---

## Implementation Plan: Restructure App with Section Navigation, New Practice Modes, and Popular Melodies

### 1. Architecture Overview

The current app has a flat navigation with 5 items. The plan keeps existing routes unchanged (Option C from the design decisions) but transforms the Header into a two-level navigation with "Drums" and "Piano" as top-level sections, each showing contextual sub-navigation. This avoids breaking bookmarks while giving the user a clear sense of being in one section or the other.

The SightReadingMode type currently has three values: `'note-drill' | 'interval' | 'phrase'`. We will extend this to five values by adding `'note-naming'` and `'melody'`. The `'mic'` input mode is orthogonal to the practice mode -- it is an *input method* not a mode, so it should be modeled as a separate `inputMethod` field on the store: `'keyboard' | 'piano-keys' | 'mic'`.

### 2. Detailed File Changes

---

#### Phase 1: Navigation Restructure

**File: `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/drum-practice/src/components/Header.tsx`**

This is the central change. Replace the flat nav array with a section-aware navigation.

Current structure:
```typescript
const nav = [
  { href: '/', label: 'Patterns' },
  { href: '/practice', label: 'Practice' },
  { href: '/live', label: 'Live' },
  { href: '/sight-reading', label: 'Sight Read' },
  { href: '/progress', label: 'Progress' },
];
```

New structure:
```typescript
type Section = 'drums' | 'piano';

const sections: { id: Section; label: string; icon: ReactNode }[] = [
  { id: 'drums', label: 'Drums', icon: /* drum circle SVG */ },
  { id: 'piano', label: 'Piano', icon: /* piano/keys SVG */ },
];

const sectionNav: Record<Section, { href: string; label: string }[]> = {
  drums: [
    { href: '/', label: 'Patterns' },
    { href: '/practice', label: 'Practice' },
    { href: '/live', label: 'Live' },
    { href: '/progress', label: 'Progress' },
  ],
  piano: [
    { href: '/sight-reading', label: 'Sight Read' },
    // Future: { href: '/piano-progress', label: 'Progress' },
  ],
};
```

Logic changes:
- Determine active section from `pathname`: if it starts with `/sight-reading`, section is `'piano'`, otherwise `'drums'`.
- Render two rows: top row has the section tabs (Drums / Piano), bottom row has the sub-nav for the active section.
- The logo text should change from "Drum Practice" to "Music Practice" (or stay neutral).
- Section tabs use a distinct style (larger, with icons) vs the sub-nav links which keep the current pill style.

Layout approach for the header:
```
| [Logo: Music Practice]    [Drums] [Piano]           |  <-- top bar (h-14)
|                   [Patterns] [Practice] [Live] [Progress] |  <-- sub-nav (h-10, only when >1 item)
```

