#### Phase 3: Microphone/Audio Input

**New file: `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/drum-practice/src/lib/audio/PitchDetector.ts`**

Core pitch detection utility using Web Audio API + autocorrelation (YIN algorithm variant).

```typescript
export class PitchDetector {
  private audioContext: AudioContext;
  private analyser: AnalyserNode;
  private stream: MediaStream | null = null;
  private source: MediaStreamAudioSourceNode | null = null;
  private buffer: Float32Array;
  private detecting: boolean = false;
  private onPitch: ((frequency: number, noteIndex: number) => void) | null = null;
  private animFrameId: number | null = null;

  constructor(audioContext: AudioContext, fftSize?: number);

  async start(): Promise<void>;
  // - Calls navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ audio: true })
  // - Creates MediaStreamAudioSourceNode -> AnalyserNode
  // - Starts requestAnimationFrame loop calling detect()

  stop(): void;
  // - Stops the stream tracks
  // - Cancels animation frame
  // - Disconnects nodes

  private detect(): void;
  // - Gets time-domain data from analyser
  // - Runs autocorrelation to find fundamental frequency
  // - If confidence is high enough, maps frequency to nearest note index
  // - Calls this.onPitch(frequency, noteIndex)

  setOnPitch(callback: (frequency: number, noteIndex: number) => void): void;
}
```

The autocorrelation algorithm:
1. Get time-domain data via `analyser.getFloatTimeDomainData(buffer)`.
2. Compute RMS to check if signal is loud enough (gate threshold ~0.01).
3. Run autocorrelation over the buffer to find the period.
4. Convert period to frequency: `frequency = sampleRate / period`.
5. Map frequency to nearest note using `ALL_NOTES` frequencies: find the note whose `frequency` is closest (within a semitone tolerance).

The frequency-to-note mapping function:
```typescript
import { ALL_NOTES } from '../sight-reading/notes';

export function frequencyToNoteIndex(freq: number): number | null {
  let bestIndex = -1;
  let bestDiff = Infinity;
  for (const note of ALL_NOTES) {
    const diff = Math.abs(1200 * Math.log2(freq / note.frequency)); // cents
    if (diff < bestDiff) {
      bestDiff = diff;
      bestIndex = note.index;
    }
  }
  // Only accept if within 50 cents (half a semitone)
  return bestDiff <= 50 ? bestIndex : null;
}
```

